      "id": "claim_36c988ef557a440096d679885afe2819",
      "statement": "The WebSocket relay authenticates MCP and extension connections with the pairing token before routing, derives an internal scope key from the token, tracks browser presence in memory only, routes MCP requests to the target browser within the authenticated scope, and returns structured errors for no browser, ambiguous target, invalid target, auth failure, invalid messages, and timeouts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0021-local-pairing-presence-routing.md#L25-L42",
